        -: 1897:/*
        -: 1898: * ===========================================================================
        -: 1899: * `V90Equalizer::process(float *, unsigned, short *, float *, unsigned &)`
        -: 1900: * -- 9,364 bytes at 0x38d80, the class's hub and the largest member of it.
        -: 1901: *
        -: 1902: * ONE CALL CARRIES A BLOCK OF RECEIVER SAMPLES THROUGH THE EQUALISER AND OUT
        -: 1903: * AS SYMBOLS.  Two input samples make one T/2-spaced symbol, so `nOut` comes
        -: 1904: * back as `n >> 1`, and an odd sample is held over to the next call in
        -: 1905: * `word_68`/`word_6c`.  Each symbol is
        -: 1906: *
        -: 1907: *      y    = linear equaliser over the delay line at `array_18`
        -: 1908: *      d    = decision-feedback filter over `array_44`
        -: 1909: *      soft = y - d
        -: 1910: *      decision = whichever slicer `state` selects
        -: 1911: *      err  = soft - decision        the DFE adapts on this
        -: 1912: *      y - decision                  the linear half adapts on THIS
        -: 1913: *
        -: 1914: * and the two errors differ by exactly `d`, so a test whose DFE output is
        -: 1915: * zero cannot tell them apart.
        -: 1916: *
        -: 1917: * EVERYTHING IS WRITTEN TWICE, BECAUSE THE EQUALISER HAS TWO REPRESENTATIONS.
        -: 1918: * `mmxMode` selects a 16-bit fixed-point form: the coefficients live as an
        -: 1919: * aligned/unaligned SHORT PAIR holding the two halves of one 32-bit
        -: 1920: * accumulator, the history lives in `array_ecAligned`, the samples are
        -: 1921: * converted into `block_b4` on the way in and the soft outputs back out of
        -: 1922: * `block_b8` on the way out.  The field is re-read from memory at every test
        -: 1923: * because it can change inside the loop -- `enterDataPhase`, `enterRRN` and
        -: 1924: * `enterFPE` can each flip it -- and the caller then re-expresses the
        -: 1925: * in-flight state in the other representation.  Those re-convert blocks are
        -: 1926: * NOT four copies of one block: one of the three forward ones truncates the
        -: 1927: * DFE output through sixteen bits and two do not, so they are three source
        -: 1928: * sites and a single helper would be wrong at exactly one of them.
        -: 1929: *
        -: 1930: * WHAT A READER SHOULD KNOW BEFORE CHANGING ANYTHING HERE:
        -: 1931: *
        -: 1932: *   - `word_20` retreats by TWO per symbol and the second step is
        -: 1933: *     UNCONDITIONAL.  The path that skips the coefficient update rejoins the
        -: 1934: *     history shift inside it, not before it, so a reading that made the
        -: 1935: *     second decrement part of the update is wrong on exactly that path.
        -: 1936: *     Finding 5700 §1.
        -: 1937: *   - `updateCoefs` is ONE variable, not two disjoint live ranges sharing a
        -: 1938: *     slot.  It starts at 1, the PHASE3 arm loads it from
